    "summary": "Delta Corp swung to a consolidated net loss of INR2.12bn (about $22.3m) for the quarter ended 30 June, against a INR294.6m profit a year earlier, driven by an exceptional INR3.07bn (about $32.1m) provision following India's Supreme Court ruling of 27 May on GST applied to online gaming, betting, gambling and casino transactions.",
    "why": "The provision breakdown - INR1.44bn of GST, INR1.48bn of interest and INR143.9m of penalty - shows interest exceeding the principal tax. Retrospective indirect tax exposure in India is compounding faster than the liability itself, which is a material factor in any India market-entry model.",
    "expanded": "Revenue from operations fell 8.5% year on year to INR1.69bn (about $17.7m), with casino gaming revenue down 12.1% to INR1.52bn and casino segment profit down 26.9% to INR199.5m. Operationally the company is shrinking its footprint: Deltin Denzong Casino in Sikkim was closed following an operational review, and King Casino was non-operational after vacating its Mandovi River location pending deployment of a new vessel. Delta says it 'continues to believe that it has strong grounds to contest' the GST calculation, interest and penalties. Taken with the Supreme Court's pending final hearings on the Promotion and Regulation of Online Gaming Act, India remains a market where the tax treatment of past revenue is as unsettled as the legality of future revenue.",
